{"uid":"8c2dffb0d249e27c","name":"test_claim_rollback_is_two_directional_by_fault_class","fullName":"tests.test_no_progress_instant_failures#test_claim_rollback_is_two_directional_by_fault_class","historyId":"be587794ed47b8af87d7c8c8dffe9242","time":{"start":1791919872162,"stop":1791919875069,"duration":2907},"description":"Task 123 (#60): the harness's pre-spawn `in-progress` claim (task\n    116) on the task a worker iteration is assigned must be rolled back to\n    the task's PRIOR status when that iteration never reaches the model at\n    all (an infra fault -- reuses the exact instant-startup-failure shape\n    the two tests above already assert the terminal state for), but must\n    be LEFT `in-progress` when the iteration genuinely reached the model\n    and failed doing real work on it (a `work` fault) -- a real, if\n    unsuccessful, attempt is not the same claim as a bet that never paid\n    off, and rolling it back too would erase that the task was actually\n    being worked on.\n\n    Two separate engine processes, each over its OWN tmp dir\n    (`engine_factory`'s own fixture reuses one `tmp_path` for every engine\n    it starts within a single test -- fine for every other test in this\n    module, which only ever starts one, but wrong here since the two\n    directions need two independent run dirs).\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 123 (#60): the harness's pre-spawn <code>in-progress</code> claim (task<br />\n116) on the task a worker iteration is assigned must be rolled back to<br />\nthe task's PRIOR status when that iteration never reaches the model at<br />\nall (an infra fault -- reuses the exact instant-startup-failure shape<br />\nthe two tests above already assert the terminal state for), but must<br />\nbe LEFT <code>in-progress</code> when the iteration genuinely reached the model<br />\nand failed doing real work on it (a <code>work</code> fault) -- a real, if<br />\nunsuccessful, attempt is not the same claim as a bet that never paid<br /